    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a high-stakes slate today, with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** standing out as the clear must-start option. With a formidable efficiency score of 80.98, he draws an ideal matchup against Junk; the combination of a favorable park factor, a strong platoon advantage, and the premier leadoff spot positions him to provide the elite stolen base production we prioritize. Similarly, **Trea Turner** offers high-end reliability with a score of 65.99. While May is a competent arm, the batting order benefit for **Trea Turner**\u2014secured in the two-hole\u2014elevates his floor, making him an essential component of our daily 5x5 attack.\n\nMid-tier decisions are dictated by SP_xERA and platoon splits, leading to a cautious approach for the remainder of the lineup. **Junior Caminero** (59.85) and **Yordan Alvarez** (57.61) remain active despite tough matchups against Fried and Gilbert, respectively; while their raw talent and spot in the batting order keep them above our 40-point threshold, their scores are suppressed by the caliber of the opposing pitching. Conversely, **Carson Benge** (47.18) and **Caleb Durbin** (48.58) are marginal plays, as their efficiency is severely hampered by negative L/L platoon matchups and difficult SP_xERA figures, leaving little room for error if they fail to contribute to our scarcity categories.\n\nThe benching process was largely dictated by external volatility rather than internal performance metrics. **Kazuma Okamoto** and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** were automatic excludes due to rainouts, while **Colt Keith** remains sidelined on the IL. With **Gary Sanchez** out of the starting lineup, the optimizer leaned heavily toward the defensive speed of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and the tactical utility of **Christian Yelich** to preserve game caps. We are proceeding without **Lars Nootbaar**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Josh Smith**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, or **Pedro Ramirez** today, as their projections did not warrant a rotation into the starting slots against the current crop of opposing arms. Keep a close eye on the weather in the **Kazuma Okamoto** game window, as any shifting systems could impact future roster availability.",
